HST Office: Sheets and chart dialogs follow the dialog layout rulebook (labels, margins, group gaps, fit).

Layout properties only in the .ui files of Format Cells (Sheets frame, Numbers, Alignment, Protection), Sort,
Standard/Advanced Filter, Insert/Delete Cells, Manage/Define Name, Data Validation, Conditional Formatting and its
manager, Sheets Page Style (Sheet and Scale pages), Headers/Footers, Row Height/Column Width, Text Import, Goal
Seek, Solver, Subtotals, Consolidate, Pivot Table, Paste Special, Protect Sheet, Duplicate Records, Sparkline,
Define Database/Table Range, Show Sheet, the Function Wizard, the chart dialogs and wizard pages, and the Statistics
and CMIS pages of Document Properties (so its tabs keep one margin); no widget, id,
label, string, order, handler or accessibility change. Values from hst::design::layout:
- a label in front of its control starts at the start of its column (xalign 0) instead of being centred or
  right-aligned;
- the inner margin is DialogMargin 12 once: tab pages and wizard step pages get 12, a dialog without tabs gets 12,
  a tabbed dialog keeps 6 around its tabs; groups stacked in one box are GroupGap 12 apart, group content is
  indented 12;
- no ellipsized label in these dialogs (Vietnamese text shows in full);
- radio buttons side by side in Handle Duplicate Records keep 12 px; the conditional-format rule summary wraps
  (at most 60 characters wide) instead of being cut.
Two size hooks in code: the Function Wizard's function list is 13 rows high instead of 15 so the wizard fits a
1366x768 screen with GTK's taller rows, and the VCL wizard places Back and Next 6 px apart (was 3) like every
other button pair. Checked by tests/unit/test_ui_layout_rulebook.py (static) and
tests/runtime/hst_dialog_layout_check.py with tests/runtime/data/dialog-layout-b.json (on screen).

